# Central admin hub (per-user tenant allowlist)

- **Hub:** `event-site-manager.com` with `NEXT_PUBLIC_ALL_TENANTS_ADMIN=true`. Public satellites keep their own domains; they must not serve `/admin`.
- **Grant `/admin` from any tenant profile** for the Clerk `userId` with `ADMIN` or `SUPER_ADMIN` — not env-tenant-only lookup. See [adminAccessServer.ts](mdc:src/app/admin/adminAccessServer.ts) and [adminTenantAccess.ts](mdc:src/lib/adminTenantAccess.ts).
- **Tenant `ADMIN`:** allowlisted `tenantId`s only. Empty `?tenant=` must become those IDs (`tenantId.equals` or `tenantId.in`), never all-tenants wildcard.
- **`SUPER_ADMIN` on the hub:** all tenants; empty filter = all.
- **Server enforcement:** use `appendAdminTenantFilter` / `resolveAdminMutationTenantId` / `headersForAdminTenantScope`. Do not trust `?tenant=` or `getTenantId()` for hub mutations.
- **Platform-only:** Tenant Management, Satellite Domains, Gas Stations, Test CRUD — `SUPER_ADMIN` only (`isPlatformOnlyAdminPath`).
- **Satellites:** `DISABLE_ADMIN_ON_SATELLITE` defaults on when `NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_IS_SATELLITE=true`; middleware redirects `/admin` to the primary hub with `?tenant=` = env tenant. Loopback and the primary host are not redirected.
- **kcnj-prod:** keep that repo’s admin fork until KCNJ operators use this hub (or merge). Same-codebase satellites share the hub now.
- **Workspace session:** After sign-in, send admins to `/admin`. List every tenant ID mapped to that Clerk user (`user_profile` ADMIN/SUPER_ADMIN rows), looking up by **userId and email** with **no env tenant pin** (`omitEnvTenantId`). Persist the pick in the httpOnly `admin_session_tenant` cookie (`__all__` only for hub SUPER_ADMIN). Filter resolution: explicit `?tenant=` → cookie → single-tenant default. Hub SUPER_ADMIN with no cookie defaults to **all tenants** (every organization is in scope); they can still pin one org from the picker.
- **Amplify hub:** `AMPLIFY_NEXT_PUBLIC_ALL_TENANTS_ADMIN=true` (and `NEXT_PUBLIC_ALL_TENANTS_ADMIN=true`) on event-site-manager.com. If this flag is missing, list APIs were previously scoped to `event_site_manager_admin_1` and the picker showed only that one card.
- **Hub SUPER_ADMIN profile:** At least one `user_profile` on `event_site_manager_admin_1` must have `user_role = SUPER_ADMIN` (ADMIN-only rows never unlock the All tenants card). Reserved emails that must stay SUPER_ADMIN across local/dev/prod export-import: `giventauser@gmail.com` and `mosc.admin.user@keleno.com`. The database repo restores them after every import (`post_import_retain_platform_super_admins.sql`, batch step 6b) so schema rebuild cannot demote or drop them.
- **Multi-tenant ADMIN:** Do not default the first of many tenants. Gate `/admin/*` subpages until they pick; `/admin` stays the picker. SUPER_ADMIN also gets an **All tenants** card.
- **Picker search + pagination:** When two or more tenant IDs are mapped (or the user is hub SUPER_ADMIN), `/admin` uses the same Tenant ID / organization-name lookup as Tenant Settings (`searchTenantOrganizationsForSelectServer`) plus the standard admin pagination footer. Pagination starts when more than 8 matching cards.
- **Change workspace:** Top tenant bar (and dashboard cards) can switch the session cookie. Do not use `appendAdminTenantFilter` when listing orgs for the picker.
- **New org admin registration:** The person registers or signs in on **that organization’s satellite** (email or Google). Hub SUPER_ADMIN then promotes the satellite `user_profile` to `ADMIN` in Manage Usage. After sign-out/in they use `event-site-manager.com/admin` and pick that org. Do not register only on the hub. Operator steps: [PROMOTE_USER_TO_ADMIN_GUIDELINES.html](mdc:public/documentation/manage_usage/PROMOTE_USER_TO_ADMIN_GUIDELINES.html).

